From: Cyryl Sochacki <cyrylsochacki@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] udev: report touchscreen pointer position and press state

In udev_input_touch_state() the RETRO_DEVICE_POINTER and
RARCH_DEVICE_POINTER_SCREEN case left the switch with a stray "break"
right after setting "screen", so the switch on the pointer id was never
reached and the pointer always reported 0 (no position, never pressed).
The menu therefore never saw touchscreen taps.

The screen check also compared against RARCH_DEVICE_MOUSE_SCREEN
instead of RARCH_DEVICE_POINTER_SCREEN, so screen coordinates were
never used for the pointer.

Tested on Allwinner A20 with an FT5x06 touchscreen, KMS + udev,
RetroArch 1.20.0 (the same code is in master).

---
--- a/input/drivers/udev_input.c
+++ b/input/drivers/udev_input.c
@@ -3081,8 +3081,7 @@
 
       case RETRO_DEVICE_POINTER:
       case RARCH_DEVICE_POINTER_SCREEN:
-         screen = (device == RARCH_DEVICE_MOUSE_SCREEN);
-         break;
+         screen = (device == RARCH_DEVICE_POINTER_SCREEN);
          switch (id)
          {
             case RETRO_DEVICE_ID_POINTER_X:
